  "problem": "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ All rational numbers are positive.",
  "worked_solution": "The given statement can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ For all $x\\in Q,$ $x$ is positive.\n\nIntroducing the universal quantifier, we get the following:\n\n$\\,$ $\u2200x\\in Q,\\,x\\text{\u00a0is positive}.$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(\u2200x\\in Q,\\,x\\text{\u00a0is positive}) & \u2261\u2203x\\in Q,\\,\u00ac(x\\text{\u00a0is positive}) \\\\  & \u2261\u2203x\\in Q,\\,x\\text{\u00a0is not positive}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich reads \n\n$\\,$ There exists $x\\in Q$ such that $x$ is not positive.\n\nor simply\n\n$\\,$ At least one rational number is not positive.",
